### ============ GET /api/auth/me ============

### With token → 200
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Without token → 401
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### Pending password change → still 200 (me is allowed)
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMustChange.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============ Policies (temporary dev endpoints) ============

### Default policy, Employee → 200
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Default policy, pending password change → 403 "password-change-required"
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMustChange.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Admin policy, Employee → 403
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Admin policy, Admin → 200
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Lockout: send "Wrong password" 5 times → the 6th attempt returns 401 "account-locked" with the wait time.
### Rate limit: more than 10 login requests within a minute from one IP → 429.

### ============ Refresh token flow (cookie "refresh_token", Path=/api/auth) ============
### The REST client keeps cookies between requests automatically. Run the requests in order.
### (The cookie is Secure: VS Code / VS send it to http://localhost; if not, pass "Cookie: refresh_token=<value>"
###  copied from the Set-Cookie header of the previous response.)

### 1. Login → 200 + Set-Cookie refresh_token (HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict; Path=/api/auth; 7 days)
# @name flowLogin
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "EMP-00004", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Refresh → 200, new access token + rotated cookie (the old token is now revoked, ReplacedByTokenId set)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### 3. Refresh with the OLD token (paste the value from step 1's Set-Cookie):
###    within 30 seconds → 401 "session-expired" only (two tabs); after 30 seconds → reuse detected:
###    401 + every active token of the user is revoked + AuditLog "RefreshToken.ReuseDetected".
###    (Only rotated tokens trigger this. A token revoked by logout or password change → 401 only.)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: refresh_token=PASTE_OLD_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_1

### 4. Logout → always 204, cookie deleted (also when the token is already revoked or missing)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout

### 5. Refresh after logout → 401 (no cookie any more)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### ============ Change password – first login (Tomer Zilber, MustChangePassword) ============

### 1. Login → 200, "mustChangePassword": true
# @name tomerLogin
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "tomer.zilber@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Any other endpoint → 403 "password-change-required"
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{tomerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 3. Refresh still works while the change is pending → 200
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### 4. Weak new password → 400 with "errors"
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{tomerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "{{password}}", "newPassword": "short" }

### 5. Wrong current password → 400 "הסיסמה הנוכחית שגויה" (audited; 5 attempts per 15 minutes per user → 429)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{tomerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "Wrong9999", "newPassword": "NewPass42" }

### 6. Valid change → 200, "mustChangePassword": false, new cookie; all older refresh tokens revoked
# @name tomerChanged
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{tomerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "{{password}}", "newPassword": "NewPass42" }

### 7. Protected endpoint with the new access token → 200
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/dev/auth/protected
Authorization: Bearer {{tomerChanged.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8. "Old phone": refresh with a cookie from before the change (paste from step 1/3's Set-Cookie)
###    → 401 only. No revoke-all: the new session from step 6 is NOT affected.
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: refresh_token=PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_BEFORE_THE_CHANGE

### 9. Refresh with the new cookie from step 6 (kept by the REST client) → still 200
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### Reset Tomer to first-login state (drops and recreates the dev database): dotnet run --project API -- --seed

