### ---------- Reset password ----------

### Reset → 200 { temporaryPassword }; MustChangePassword, lockout cleared, all refresh tokens revoked
# @name reset
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/{{created.response.body.$.user.id}}/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The session from before the reset is gone: refresh with the cookie of "createdLogin" → 401
### (paste it from the Set-Cookie of createdLogin if the REST client replaced it since)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh

### The new temporary password works → 200 (the previous one → 401)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "{{created.response.body.$.user.employeeCode}}", "password": "{{reset.response.body.$.temporaryPassword}}" }

### Resetting your own password → 422 (use change-password)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/24/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ---------- Activate / deactivate ----------

### Deactivate yourself → 422 "self-deactivation"
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/24/active
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### Deactivate a department manager (Ron) → 422 "department-manager-deactivation"
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/3/active
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### Deactivate a handler (Liat) → 200, unassignedTicketCount = her unresolved tickets, back in the department queue
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/10/active
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### Liat can no longer sign in → 401
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "liat.shahar@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Reactivate Liat → 200, unassignedTicketCount 0 (her tickets are not given back automatically)
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/10/active
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": true }

### Missing isActive → 400, errors.isActive
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/10/active
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ }

### ---------- Last active admin ----------
### Reachable only with a stale token: 1) Yael makes Adi an admin, 2) Adi signs in, 3) Yael removes Admin from Adi
### (the access token of Adi still says Admin for up to 15 minutes), 4) Adi removes Admin from Yael → 422 "last-admin".

### 1. Adi becomes Admin
PUT {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/25
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "עדי", "lastName": "שמעוני", "email": "adi.shimoni@example.com", "departmentId": 6, "jobTitle": "רכזת משאבי אנוש", "roles": ["Handler", "Admin"] }

### 2. Adi signs in
# @name adi
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "adi.shimoni@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 3. Yael removes Admin from Adi → 200 (Yael remains an active admin)
PUT {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/25
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "עדי", "lastName": "שמעוני", "email": "adi.shimoni@example.com", "departmentId": 6, "jobTitle": "רכזת משאבי אנוש", "roles": ["Handler"] }

### 4. Adi (stale Admin token) removes Admin from Yael → 422 "last-admin"
PUT {{API_HostAddress}}/api/users/24
Authorization: Bearer {{adi.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "יעל", "lastName": "הרפז", "email": "yael.harpaz@example.com", "departmentId": 6, "jobTitle": "מנהלת משאבי אנוש", "roles": ["Handler", "DepartmentManager"] }

